From e9aef9df856e1dead626119f946795df436ae114 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 10:07:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-196: Design B BUILT - heterogeneous split-k FA
 (per-query source selection), the Vulkan dispatch

Shaders (all three FA variants): k_num keeps ONLY its index-decode duty; new push constants
k_base/k_total replace it in every scratch offset AND the store-path selector (lane-195 trap #1 -
a 1-partition ring dispatch must take the split epilogue or it is silently dropped);
m_width/mask_col_base decouple the mask stride from the dispatch's own KV (trap #2), folded into
m_offset so zero mask read sites change. Push block 128->144 B; devices below sizeof are refused
FA in supports_op (Vulkan's 128-B floor is the portability minimum, the 780M reports 256).

Dispatch: ggml_vk_flash_attn gains one defaulted part arg (forced common gqa - the gqa/non-gqa
epilogues index the shared scratch differently, so partitions must agree; aligned forced false,
mask-opt refused+asserted, dequant-kv refused: partitions are read IN PLACE); split-k heuristic
extracted to ONE home so the wrapper's k_total cannot disagree with the body dispatch;
ggml_vk_flash_attn_segmented = body(q4_0, own split-k) + ring hi + ring lo (F16, 1 partition
each), ONE reduce with k_num=k_total. Mask column bases DERIVED from row counts everywhere.

Graph (opt-in LLAMA_KV_TAIL_PERQ=1, NORING wins): tail_compose stashes RAW ring views and
returns the bare body view [0,split) - nothing materialised, nothing converted, ggml_concat
gone from the graph; fa_attach_segments permutes+attaches on the FA node via a memory-context
virtual (turbo precedent; hybrid forwards). Fallback is the shipped compose, never body-only.
One-time WARN receipt 'PER-QUERY ACTIVE'; the tail banner names mode=per-query|compose.

Gate: test-fa-segments grew LEG V - the same split-equivalence/poison/mixed-dtype legs on the
GPU backend, BOTH broadcast shapes (gqa scratch-layout agreement is the one new risk),
EXECUTED-asserted (56 GPU cases; DECLINED=FAIL). CPU legs 0-3 unchanged and green (leg 1 still
nmse=0 exactly). V1 tolerance is 1e-5 not 0: coinciding partition boundaries are bit-identical,
differing groupings round the f16 O-accumulator differently (~1e-7..1e-6), the control fires at
>=0.017 - the discriminating fidelity leg is V3 vs the independent in-file reference (all 12
mixed cases ~1e-6 vs tol 5e-4). arifi_sync_check OK.

Design-origin: BeeLlama kvarn_flash_attn.comp (one fp32 online softmax over two sources,
lane-174); ours reaches the same softmax through the EXISTING flash_attn_split_k_reduce.
